woman, not part of one.

1963
01:26:28,716 --> 01:26:30,185
- [Mike] Well, enough
yapping. I better get at it.

1964
01:26:30,185 --> 01:26:32,287
- Is it a crime to
want to keep you alive?

1965
01:26:35,156 --> 01:26:37,492
Is it a crime for science
to jump ahead by years?

1966
01:26:37,492 --> 01:26:39,360
- Here, keep yourself
busy with that.

1967
01:26:40,461 --> 01:26:42,130
- This kind of
thing must be done.

1968
01:26:44,666 --> 01:26:46,134
When it's over, you'll see.

1969
01:26:46,134 --> 01:26:47,602
- [Mike] Look, in a week,
we'll be laughing about this.

1970
01:26:47,602 --> 01:26:49,170
- I've got to hurry now.

1971
01:26:50,371 --> 01:26:52,373
The drug will wear off
soon, she'll be awake.

1972
01:26:54,776 --> 01:26:56,144
When she does come to.

1973
01:26:56,144 --> 01:26:57,912
- She's going to blow her top.

1974
01:26:57,912 --> 01:27:01,049
- It will be your head
consciously awakening for her.

1975
01:27:01,049 --> 01:27:02,717
- [Tom] Well, for
you, more like.

1976
01:27:05,019 --> 01:27:07,255
- First, how 'bout
a Pop-Tart, huh?

1977
01:27:07,255 --> 01:27:10,091
- [Tom] You're telling me
you could say no to those?

1978
01:27:10,091 --> 01:27:11,759
- [Mike] I like 'em.

1979
01:27:12,927 --> 01:27:15,063
Put a Libbyland dinner
in here. It saves time.

1980
01:27:20,268 --> 01:27:23,004
- I wish my assistant hadn't
had his arms pulled off.

1981
01:27:23,004 --> 01:27:24,572
Things would move a lot faster.

1982
01:27:28,409 --> 01:27:29,677
- [Mike] I got some Wartex here.

1983
01:27:29,677 --> 01:27:31,346
I hope it works
on the whole head.

1984
01:27:36,017 --> 01:27:38,019
- You, you must be stopped.

1985
01:27:38,019 --> 01:27:39,988
- [Tom] Like a microwave
Brenda Vaccaro.

1986
01:27:39,988 --> 01:27:41,489
- You must.

1987
01:27:41,489 --> 01:27:42,724
- And who's going to do it?

1988
01:27:42,724 --> 01:27:44,425
- Super Skull gonna
jump out and bite me?

1989
01:27:46,694 --> 01:27:48,363
- You can't stop me.

1990
01:27:49,264 --> 01:27:50,798
- [Bill] Very well.

1991
01:27:50,798 --> 01:27:53,735
- Ah, thank you!
- Thank you!

1992
01:27:53,735 --> 01:27:55,570
- [Mike] Patty Hearst.

1993
01:28:01,743 --> 01:28:04,445
- [Tom] I think I'll
shoot a little pool first.

1994
01:28:06,481 --> 01:28:10,485
(Crow mimicking muffled speech)

1995
01:28:15,990 --> 01:28:17,659
(creature knocking)

1996
01:28:17,659 --> 01:28:18,993
- [Tom] Points of Law!

1997
01:28:25,500 --> 01:28:26,834
(creature knocking)

1998
01:28:26,834 --> 01:28:29,103
- [Mike] Look, you were
just out an hour ago.

1999
01:28:33,174 --> 01:28:34,676
- Fine, fine.

2000
01:28:34,676 --> 01:28:36,377
I'll just do my
little operation later

2001
01:28:36,377 --> 01:28:38,880
because the thing in the
closet has gotta go out.

2002
01:28:40,348 --> 01:28:42,550
- [Tom] Now, this could be
the single stupidest thing

2003
01:28:42,550 --> 01:28:43,951
that clown has ever
done in his life.

2004
01:28:43,951 --> 01:28:45,953
And he's done some
pretty stupid things.

2005
01:28:51,859 --> 01:28:53,895
- [Mike] (humming) Well,
there seems to be no need

2006
01:28:53,895 --> 01:28:55,163
to move away from this door.

2007
01:28:55,163 --> 01:28:56,798
I can see no reason
at all in the world

2008
01:28:56,798 --> 01:28:59,500
why I shouldn't just stand
right here in front of, oh!

2009
01:29:01,669 --> 01:29:03,571
- You have a kind face.

2010
01:29:08,376 --> 01:29:09,911
- [Tom] Should've
used stronger bolts.

2011
01:29:09,911 --> 01:29:11,913
Pat Summerall, you betrayed me!

2012
01:29:14,349 --> 01:29:15,750
- [Mike] Ooh, Boo Radley.

2013
01:29:17,352 --> 01:29:19,487
- I think he's more horrible.

2014
01:29:20,655 --> 01:29:21,456
- [Tom] I still
go with the head.

2015
01:29:21,456 --> 01:29:22,390
Mike, how about you?

2016
01:29:22,390 --> 01:29:23,958
- [Mike] Um, I don't know.

2017
01:29:23,958 --> 01:29:27,362
- [Tom] You don't
have to choose.

2018
01:29:27,362 --> 01:29:30,365
- This is why I'm under lock
and key. I can't be trusted.

2019
01:29:31,499 --> 01:29:33,201
- [Tom] Especially
good neck juice today.

2020
01:29:33,201 --> 01:29:34,836
- [Mike] Look, you
know your business,

2021
01:29:34,836 --> 01:29:37,305
but if you just move the
door, you could kill me.

2022
01:29:39,607 --> 01:29:41,576
- Does this bug you,
does this bug you?

2023
01:29:42,577 --> 01:29:45,480
(Bill screaming)

2024
01:29:45,480 --> 01:29:46,714
- [Tom] There, you see?
Now you're free to kill me.

2025
01:29:46,714 --> 01:29:49,350
You can even use the
door if you want.

2026
01:29:49,350 --> 01:29:51,419
- [Mike] Having no
hands really bites.

2027
01:29:54,122 --> 01:29:55,590
- Marble edges light quickly.

2028
01:30:00,661 --> 01:30:03,664
(suspenseful music)

2029
01:30:05,133 --> 01:30:07,635
- [Mike] Hey, come here.
Buddy, I'll book you in Iowa.

2030
01:30:07,635 --> 01:30:08,469
Come here.

2031
01:30:10,471 --> 01:30:11,472
- [Mike] Ew.

2032
01:30:14,509 --> 01:30:18,146
- [Tom] I thought that
would taste better.

2033
01:30:18,146 --> 01:30:19,781
- [Mike] That is one
bad McNugget. Ugh.

2034
01:30:21,682 --> 01:30:24,919
- [Tom] Can I have that back?
I kinda need it, it's my neck.

2035
01:30:28,489 --> 01:30:30,258
- He's got his
lounging jammies on.

2036
01:30:31,993 --> 01:30:33,394
- [Tom] Help, I'm in
another dimension, help.

2037
01:30:34,996 --> 01:30:35,830
Help?

2038
01:30:43,538 --> 01:30:46,040
- [Mike] Look at that. The
mask is just tied in the back.

2039
01:30:46,040 --> 01:30:48,209
- [Tom] It's nothing we
haven't seen before, Mike.

2040
01:30:49,410 --> 01:30:50,578
- He's got a soggy butt.

2041
01:30:53,881 --> 01:30:55,349
- [Tom] Hey, pal, what about me?

2042
01:30:55,349 --> 01:30:56,884
Your friend, the head, remember?

2043
01:30:56,884 --> 01:30:57,852
Oh, you jerk.

2044
01:30:57,852 --> 01:31:00,254
- I told you to let me die.

2045
01:31:01,189 --> 01:31:03,458
- Men just never listen.

2046
01:31:03,458 --> 01:31:05,359
(Jan laughing)

2047
01:31:05,359 --> 01:31:06,194
- [Mike] Oh, I get it.

2048
01:31:06,194 --> 01:31:07,528
It was a comedy.

2049
01:31:07,528 --> 01:31:11,032
- [Tom] Always leave
'em laughing. (laughing)

2050
01:31:12,333 --> 01:31:13,835
- [Mike] Let's get outta here.

2051
01:31:13,835 --> 01:31:15,903
- No, they mean the brain
that wouldn't die. The end.

2052
01:31:32,320 --> 01:31:35,389
- So you guys, we watched the
cheesy movie and now what?

2053
01:31:35,389 --> 01:31:38,226
We just stand around
being depressed?

2054
01:31:38,226 --> 01:31:39,694
- Heck no.

2055
01:31:39,694 --> 01:31:42,230
Now's the time we usually open
up a big batch of letters.

2056
01:31:42,230 --> 01:31:44,031
- Yeah, Mike, the love and
affection of the viewers

2057
01:31:44,031 --> 01:31:46,467
will automatically make
you feel much better.

2058
01:31:46,467 --> 01:31:48,236
Dig deep in that pile.

2059
01:31:48,236 --> 01:31:49,737
- None of these are for me.

2060
01:31:49,737 --> 01:31:50,905
- Oh.

2061
01:31:50,905 --> 01:31:52,840
- Hey, someone's
calling on the Hexfield!

2062
01:31:52,840 --> 01:31:54,208
- Thank goodness.

2063
01:31:54,208 --> 01:31:55,409
- Oh, hey everyone!

2064
01:31:55,409 --> 01:31:57,044
It's Jan from
today's experiment!

2065
01:31:57,044 --> 01:31:59,113
Geez, we thought you had
perished in that fire.

2066
01:31:59,113 --> 01:32:00,414
- Oh, I haven't, no.

2067
01:32:00,414 --> 01:32:03,184
I survived that ordeal
and many others too.

2068
01:32:03,184 --> 01:32:05,486
Hey, I just wanted to call
you a nice young gentlemen

2069
01:32:05,486 --> 01:32:07,188
and tell you I'm
feeling much better now.

2070
01:32:07,188 --> 01:32:08,856
I didn't want you to worry.

2071
01:32:08,856 --> 01:32:10,157
- [Mike] Oh, so you're
not into that whole

2072
01:32:10,157 --> 01:32:12,159
"Let me die, please let
me die" thing any more?

2073
01:32:12,159 --> 01:32:13,394
- Oh, of course not.

2074
01:32:13,394 --> 01:32:15,730
That was just a phase
I was going through.

2075
01:32:15,730 --> 01:32:18,866
You know, when my head
was first lopped off it,

2076
01:32:18,866 --> 01:32:21,202
it was kind of a
difficult time for me.

2077
01:32:21,202 --> 01:32:24,438
- [Crow] Yeah, you must have
really gone to your head.

2078
01:32:24,438 --> 01:32:27,074
- [Mike] Hey, Crow,
that's not nice.

2079
01:32:27,074 --> 01:32:28,309
- Oh, that's okay.

2080
01:32:28,309 --> 01:32:30,978
Believe you me, I have
heard it all before.

2081
01:32:30,978 --> 01:32:34,348
Those jokes usually leave
me rolling in the aisle.

2082
01:32:34,348 --> 01:32:35,182
Literally!

2083
01:32:35,182 --> 01:32:36,851
(all laughing)

2084
01:32:36,851 --> 01:32:38,452
- [Mike] So what have you
been up to all these years?

2085
01:32:38,452 --> 01:32:41,522
- Well, at first it was
kind of hard to find work,

2086
01:32:41,522 --> 01:32:42,957
as you can well imagine.

2087
01:32:42,957 --> 01:32:45,626
Then I finally got
a job as a doorstop.

2088
01:32:45,626 --> 01:32:47,028
It doesn't pay much,

2089
01:32:47,028 --> 01:32:49,063
but at least I've
regained my self-respect.

2090
01:32:49,063 --> 01:32:50,698
- [Tom] So do you get out much?

2091
01:32:50,698 --> 01:32:52,066
- Oh, you bet.

2092
01:32:52,066 --> 01:32:53,301
I love to go out to eat.

2093
01:32:53,301 --> 01:32:56,771
Hey, I can eat all
the cheesecake I want,

2094
01:32:56,771 --> 01:32:59,006
it goes straight to
my hips but who cares?

2095
01:32:59,006 --> 01:33:01,542
(all laughing)

2096
01:33:01,542 --> 01:33:03,044
And I love parties.

2097
01:33:03,044 --> 01:33:05,246
You know, after I've had
a couple of drinks in me,

2098
01:33:05,246 --> 01:33:08,182
my Jeffrey says I'm the
mouth that wouldn't die.

2099
01:33:08,182 --> 01:33:09,650
(all laughing)

2100
01:33:09,650 --> 01:33:10,885
- [Crow] Oh, so you're married.

2101
01:33:10,885 --> 01:33:13,754
- Oh yes. Jeff and
I are so happy.

2102
01:33:13,754 --> 01:33:16,691
He even bought me this new pan.

2103
01:33:16,691 --> 01:33:19,160
I guess you could
say our relationship

2104
01:33:19,160 --> 01:33:20,761
has really panned out.

2105
01:33:20,761 --> 01:33:23,731
(all laughing)

2106
01:33:23,731 --> 01:33:25,633
- [Mike] It's great that you
got a sense of humor about it.

2107
01:33:25,633 --> 01:33:28,536
And so I want to ask when
you were in that fire,

2108
01:33:28,536 --> 01:33:30,037
did you make your own gravy?

2109
01:33:31,939 --> 01:33:33,774
- So what are you saying?

2110
01:33:33,774 --> 01:33:35,977
- [Mike] Well, it
was just a joke.

2111
01:33:35,977 --> 01:33:38,779
- Well, I fail to see the humor.

2112
01:33:38,779 --> 01:33:40,715
Well, I guess I better be going.

2113
01:33:44,251 --> 01:33:46,687
- Oh, good one, Mike.

2114
01:33:46,687 --> 01:33:49,290
- You know, guys,
the whole situation,

2115
01:33:49,290 --> 01:33:53,527
being stuck up here in space,
forced to watch cheesy movies,

2116
01:33:53,527 --> 01:33:56,263
interacting with
other life forms,

2117
01:33:56,263 --> 01:33:57,565
it kinda bites.

2118
01:33:57,565 --> 01:34:00,134
- You're starting to
catch on, Kemosabe.

2119
01:34:00,134 --> 01:34:01,268
What do you think, sirs?

2120
01:34:02,737 --> 01:34:06,540
- Hmm, a head in a pan. What
a fabulous idea. (laughing)

2121
01:34:06,540 --> 01:34:08,643
- Well, sir, should I
file the experiment?

2122
01:34:11,278 --> 01:34:14,749
Oh well, here we go again.

2123
01:34:14,749 --> 01:34:17,685
(chainsaw whirring)

2124
01:34:17,685 --> 01:34:20,421
(sweeping music)

2125
01:35:19,547 --> 01:35:23,384
- Who's to tell me to
blow if I don't want to?

2126
01:35:26,721 --> 01:35:28,189
- [Announcer] This has
been a presentation

2127
01:35:28,189 --> 01:35:29,890
from Comedy Central.

